WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:09.311
Agent Team Debugger: a re-implementation of AGDebugger, CHI 2025, with error-anchored context. Nguyen Nhat Minh and Do Duc Anh.

2
00:00:10.555 --> 00:00:21.019
A developer opens a failing run: the team was asked for an observatory's financial-year visitors per instrument, and after 228 runtime messages gave no answer.

3
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:26.274
Scrolling to the end: the orchestrator re-planned twenty-two times and gave up.

4
00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:37.445
The overview maps the whole session: one rectangle per message, coloured by type, sender or recipient; a click jumps the history to it.

5
00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:48.025
Rather than read everything, the developer opens the error context panel: a judge pass over the session, run once and stored with the recording.

6
00:00:48.331 --> 00:00:53.923
Five ranked suspects appear in the panel, the overview and on the cards, each with a reason.

7
00:00:54.294 --> 00:01:03.630
Selecting one assembles its context: who said what to that agent, the tool calls before it, warnings, cited evidence, and a suggested edit.

8
00:01:04.661 --> 00:01:10.541
One click opens the editor on that message, pre-filled with the original text and the suggestion.

9
00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:18.494
The developer rewrites the instruction: read both monthly visitor reports and the facilities page; do not look for annual accounts.

10
00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:27.969
Save edit and revert restores all agents to the checkpoint before this message and forks a new session, which then continues live.

11
00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:48.319
The finished branch, saved from a live continuation of this edit: the same team sums the monthly tables and answers 6651.7. Both sessions stay side by side, the failing one with its suspect markers.

12
00:01:49.164 --> 00:01:56.340
Agent Team Debugger: history, reset-and-edit, overview and error-anchored context on AutoGen and React.
